  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#syntax-attribute-name\r\n\r\n> In the HTML syntax, attribute names, even those for foreign elements, may be written with any mix of ASCII lower and ASCII upper alphas.\r\n\r\nThis could be read to mean that attribute names may only be ASCII lower and upper alphas (not numbers etc etc). I believe the intent is something like:\r\n\r\nIf the document is an [HTML document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document), attribute names are considered equivalent if they are an [ASCII case-insensitive](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive) match.\r\n\r\n",
